13194139535906 true] [17592186373796 1113 #uuid "e51fe277-17dd-59c2-bd43-427728072d61" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373796 1145 "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nC={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nD={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $C∖D$ is the *difference* of $C$ and $D,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $C$ but *not* in $D.$\n\nThe elements of $C$ that are also in $D$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}-{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373798 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373799 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373800 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373801 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373802 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1041 "selection" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373799 13194139535906 true] [17592186373797 1110 #uuid "3f57eac1-42c3-57be-8825-0fb0d6c2c319" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373798 1034 "{10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373798 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535906 true] [17592186373798 1111 #uuid "dfd2fced-4366-5e8e-84e6-0b9bbe451fde" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373799 1034 "∅" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373799 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535906 true] [17592186373799 1111 #uuid "ca41bfe1-2185-5f8b-8871-3f8a6ffa3082" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373800 1034 "{15,30,45,60,75,…}" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535906 true] [17592186373800 1111 #uuid "bbc97d2a-2bb3-50cb-9609-da058b25ee34" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373801 1034 "{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373801 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535906 true] [17592186373801 1111 #uuid "5cbf96d1-db2a-5f99-af14-f66f0b10ea22" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373802 1034 "{5,15,25,35,45,55,65,75,…}" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535906 true] [17592186373802 1111 #uuid "fdc7be85-8623-5c7b-a5b1-4833b2027095" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373803 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373804 13194139535906 true] [17592186373803 1089 "q-81518" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373803 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535906 true] [17592186373803 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/a2cee4b60fe7cf45df5cca5c0d513c38f6639b08486272d9cb4e605b8359935c.png)\n\nGiven the sets $A={d,i,f,e,r}$ and $B={f,e,r,a,k},$ find $B∖A.$" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373803 1113 #uuid "a4745e1e-8ed1-5691-b0d7-67c4f8ae24ed" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373803 1145 "The difference $B∖A$ consists of all the elements that are in $B$ but not $A.$ To represent $B∖A,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $B$ but not $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/7ec40584f82d7bd01aa7323ffb9cc4a53d631b74ea1d312d1b4141eb5da8d0d9.png)\n\nThe elements $a$ and $k$ are in $B$ but not $A.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nB∖A={a,k}.\n$$" 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373805 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373806 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373807 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373808 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373809 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535906 true] [17592186373804 1041 "selection" 13194139535906 true] [17592